          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            finds its natural general formulation in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
            in an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} sheaf cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            Therefore to amplify that one is looking at general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            without restricting to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian cohomology
            one speaks of
            = succeed "." do
              %strong nonabelian cohomology
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            To say this in a bit more detail (following
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+Character+Map+in+Equivariant+Twistorial+Cohomotopy"} SS24
          %h3#CohomologyViaClassifyingSpaces Cohomology via classifying spaces
          %p
            It is a classical and yet possibly undervalued fact that
            %em
              reasonable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
              theories have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            (and more generally
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} classifying stacks
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS23"} FSS23, §2
          %p
            %strong Ordinary cohomology.
            This begins with the observation that (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology"}> reduced
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spaces"} Eilenberg-MacLane spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n)
            – in that on well-behaved topological spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            between the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            of the respective (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"}> pointed
            )
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
