                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Street-Conspectus.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4419-1524-5"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4419-1524-5
          %p
            Parallel to this development of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent and codescent
            there was the development of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+cohomology+theory"} homotopical cohomology theory
            as described in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+S.+Brown"}> Kenneth S. Brown
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abstract Homotopy Theory and Generalized Sheaf Cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/schreiber/Abstract%20homotopy%20theory%20and%20generalized%20sheaf%20cohomology.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The two approaches are different, but closely related. Their relation is via the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} codescent
          %p There is a chain of inclusions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AbelianGroups
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ChainComplexesOfAbelianGroups
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi CrossedComplexes
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ω
                  %mi Groupoids
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ω
                  %mi Categories
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  AbelianGroups \hookrightarrow
                  ChainComplexesOfAbelianGroups
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  CrossedComplexes
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\omega Groupoids
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\omega Categories
          %p
            along which one can generalize the coefficient objects of ordinary cohomology. (See
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-groupoid"} strict omega-groupoid
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-category"} strict omega-category
            = succeed "." do
              %em nonabelian cohomology
          %p
            Depending on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} models
            chosen, there are different concrete realizations of nonabelian cohomology.
          %p
            For instance nonabelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cohomology"} Čech cohomology
            played a special role in the motivation of the notion of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe+%28in+nonabelian+cohomology%29"} gerbe (in nonabelian cohomology)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            methods dominate the discussion of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
          %p
            Either way, one obtains a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                cohomology on
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-catgories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
          %p
            This is conceptually best understood today in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} higher topos theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaves"} (infinity,1)-categories of (infinity,1)-sheaves
          %p
            This perspective on nonabelian cohomology is discussed for instance in
            %a{:href => "#Toen02"} Toen 02
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#postnikov_decomposition_and_whitehead_principle Postnikov decomposition and Whitehead principle
          %p
            In an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            every object has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} Postnikov tower in an (∞,1)-category
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Toen02"} Toën
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+principle+of+nonabelian+cohomology"} Whitehead principle of nonabelian cohomology
          %h2#special_cases Special cases
          %h3#nonabelian_group_cohomology Nonabelian group cohomology
          %p
            Sometimes the term
            %em nonabelian cohomology
            is used in a more restrictive sense. Often people mean
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group+cohomology"} nonabelian group cohomology
            when they say nonabelian cohomology, hence restricting to the domains to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoids
            with a single object.
          %p This kind of nonabelian cohomology is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+n-Categories+and+Cohomology"} Lectures on n-Categories and Cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0608420"}> arXiv
              ).
          %p
            That and how ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            is reproduced from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+cohomology+theory"} homotopical cohomology theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-groupoid"} strict omega-groupoids
            is discussed in detail in chapter 12 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie Brown
              , P. Higgins, R. Sivera,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+algebraic+topology"} Nonabelian algebraic topology
          %p For more see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group+cohomology"}> nonabelian group cohomology
              \.
          %h3#NonabelianSheafCohomology Nonabelian sheaf cohomology with constant coefficients
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is to define it as the intrinsic cohomology as seen in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(X,A)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\pi_0 Top(X, |A|) \simeq \pi_0 \infty Func(Sing X, A)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |A|
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sing X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            But both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            here naturally can be regarded, in several ways, as objects of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} = Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
            over nontrivial
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian sheaf cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            such that the corresponding nonabelian sheaf cohomology coincides with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(X,A)
            (for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h4#petit_sheaf_topos
            Petit
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            equipped with the canonical structure of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  Sh_{(\infty,1)}(Op(X))
          %p
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            itself is naturally identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = * \in Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/petit+topos"} petit topos
            incarnation of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi LConst
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (LConst \dashv \Gamma) :  Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
                  \\stackrel{\overset{LConst}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}
                  \\infty Grpd
          %p
            be the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} constant (∞,1)-sheaf
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LConst
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LConst
            an an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \infty Grpd
            is regarded as an object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LConst
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LConst A \in Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
          %p
            There is therefore the
            %em intrinsic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of the
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
            with coefficients in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} constant (∞,1)-sheaf
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi LConst
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H'(X,A)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\pi_0 Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)(X, LConst A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+with+constant+coefficients"} cohomology with constant coefficients
          %p
            Notice that since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is in fact the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
            and that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)(X,-)
            is in fact that
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Γ
                  %mi LConst
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq \pi_0 \Gamma LConst A
                  \\,.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} constant coefficients
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \infty Grpd
              agree:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sing
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi LConst
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H(X,A)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\pi_0 \infty Grpd(Sing X,A)  \simeq Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)(X,LConst A)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, theorem 7.1.0.1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            for more.
          %h4#gros_sheaf_topos
            Gros
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Another alternative is to regard the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as an object in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETop%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ETop∞Grpd
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ETop
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi LConst
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Π
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi \dashv LConst \dashv \Gamma)
                  \:
                  ETop\infty Grpd
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{LConst}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}}
                  \\infty Grpd
                  \\,,
          %p
            with the further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LConst
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LConst
            being the intrinsic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+in+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid in a locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            functor. The intrinsic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            in there also coincides with nonabelian cohomology in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              we have an equivalence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ETop
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi LConst
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ETop\infty Grpd(X, LConst A)
                    \\simeq
                    Top(X, |A|)
            %p and hence in particular an isomorphism on cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi ETop
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi LConst
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H(X,A) \simeq \pi_0   ETop\infty Grpd(X, LConst A)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              See
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETop%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ETop∞Grpd
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Examples of
            %em generalized
            nonabelian cohomology (with general classifying spaces):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+topological+K-theory"} unstable topological K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"} Cohomotopy
          %h2#objects_classified_by_nonabelian_cohomology Objects classified by nonabelian cohomology
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : X \to A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in nonabelian cohomology, we say the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+sequence"} homotopy fibers
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is the object
            %em classified
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          %p For examples and discussion of this see
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"}> principal 2-bundle
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+3-bundle"}> principal 3-bundle
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-gerbe"} 2-gerbe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"}> principal ∞-bundle
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-gerbe"} ∞-gerbe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+form"} twisted forms
                \.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} nonabelian Poincaré duality
            %li
              %p
